That's because the `rewrites` are wrong. You should return the `test-static` part as dynamic, and make sure `getStaticPaths` return it correctly.

```js
export const getStaticPaths: GetStaticPaths = async () => {
  return {
    paths: [
      {
        params: {
          "test-static": "test-statique",
          id: "123", // This is the default `id` of the test page.
        },
        locale: "fr",
      },
    ],
    fallback: "blocking",
  }
}
```

And just remove the rewrite.

Thanks for pointing out the missing documentation, I'll note the team.

On the second look, I don't think you actually need to define the paths in `getStaticPaths` though.

This will work all the same:
```js
export const getStaticPaths: GetStaticPaths = async () => {
  return {
    paths: [],
    fallback: "blocking",
  }
}
```

Any request to `/fr/...` will indicate Next.js that you are on `router.locale === "fr"`

The important part is to make `test-static` dynamic since it is changing.

@balazsorban44 yes, the example is probably not a good one for static paths since it uses an `id` but I was just trying to reproduce the behavior. 

If we imagine another example where you have possibly 2-3 valid values for the parameter and would like to statically generate these pages for speed, then from what you are saying you would need to include the path for each locale as passing the parameter only will not work.

In my scenario this would be quite fragile since the URLs are managed elsewhere - maybe I should re-open this ticket under a new feature but it looks like a potential unlikely edge-case with debatable value :)

Oh one last thing, when I replace `getStaticPaths` and `getStaticProps` by 

```
export const getServerSideProps: GetServerSideProps = async () => {
  return { props: {} }; // Empty properties, since we are only using this to get the query parameters.
};
```

The SSR for `/fr/test-statique/123` correctly hydrates `asPath` with `/test-statique/123` and matches the client side value too.

This would be the behavior I would expect when using `getStaticPaths` and `getStaticProps`.
